WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.826
Gate three is Oracle Cloud Infrastructure,

2
00:00:02.826 --> 00:00:06.912
and it matters here because the
HR platform runs on Oracle Cloud.

3
00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:10.036
Reading that tenancy's
announcements means platform

4
00:00:10.036 --> 00:00:13.437
maintenance reaches the HR
system's owners before it lands.

5
00:00:13.437 --> 00:00:18.074
Oracle publishes maintenance, changes,
action-required notices and production

6
00:00:18.074 --> 00:00:22.088
events as announcements, and updates
to one announcement form a chain.

7
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.987
The kit keeps only the
latest in each chain.

8
00:00:24.987 --> 00:00:28.110
Oracle's documentation
gives the policy statement:

9
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.813
allow the reader's group to read
announcements in the tenancy.

10
00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:35.861
Read, not inspect, because
inspect lists summaries only,

11
00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:38.237
without the affected resources.

12
00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:41.925
Then cross-check with Oracle's
own list command, and collect.

13
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:45.931
For government, Oracle's US
Government Cloud page lists the

14
00:00:45.931 --> 00:00:50.263
Announcements endpoints in two
regions, in the realm called OC2.

15
00:00:50.263 --> 00:00:53.009
The third realm's
endpoint isn't specified,

16
00:00:53.009 --> 00:00:57.380
because Oracle's page wasn't readable,
so the kit refuses that realm.
